{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"debounce-throttle","title":"Debounce & Throttle","group":"Advanced Concepts","order":51,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Two ways to rate-limit a function that fires too often (typing, scrolling, resizing): <strong>debounce</strong> waits for quiet, <strong>throttle</strong> runs at most once per interval.</p>\n<div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-player-pause\"></i>Debounce</h3><p>Run only after the calls have <strong>stopped</strong> for <code>wait</code> ms. Every new call resets the timer. → search-as-you-type, auto-save, resize end.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-gauge\"></i>Throttle</h3><p>Run at most <strong>once every</strong> <code>wait</code> ms, no matter how often it is called. → scroll position, mouse move, rate-limited APIs.</p></div></div>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-code\"></i>Debounce</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function debounce(fn, wait) {\n  let timer;\n  return function (...args) {\n    clearTimeout(timer);\n    timer = setTimeout(() =&gt; fn.apply(this, args), wait);\n  };\n}\n\nconst search = debounce((q) =&gt; console.log(\"searching for:\", q), 30);\nsearch(\"j\");\nsearch(\"ja\");\nsearch(\"jav\");                          // only this one survives the burst\nsetTimeout(() =&gt; search(\"javascript\"), 60);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>searching for: jav\nsearching for: javascript</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-code\"></i>Throttle</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function throttle(fn, wait) {\n  let last = 0, timer = null, pendingArgs = null;\n  return function (...args) {\n    const now = Date.now();\n    const remaining = wait - (now - last);\n    if (remaining &lt;= 0) {               // leading call\n      last = now;\n      fn.apply(this, args);\n    } else {                            // remember the latest call for the trailing edge\n      pendingArgs = args;\n      timer ??= setTimeout(() =&gt; {\n        last = Date.now();\n        timer = null;\n        fn.apply(this, pendingArgs);\n      }, remaining);\n    }\n  };\n}\n\nconst onScroll = throttle((y) =&gt; console.log(\"handle scroll at\", y), 50);\nonScroll(0);                  // runs immediately (leading edge)\nonScroll(10);                 // ignored…\nonScroll(20);                 // …but the latest is kept for the trailing edge</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>handle scroll at 0\nhandle scroll at 20</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Debounce</th><th>Throttle</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Runs</td><td>Once, after the burst ends</td><td>Regularly during the burst</td></tr><tr><td>Guarantee</td><td>Latest value, eventually</td><td>At most one call per <code>wait</code></td></tr><tr><td>Typical use</td><td>Search box, validation, auto-save</td><td>Scroll, resize, drag, analytics</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p>Production versions (lodash <code>debounce</code>/<code>throttle</code>) add <code>leading</code>/<code>trailing</code> options, <code>cancel()</code> and <code>flush()</code>. Remember to cancel pending timers when a component unmounts.</p></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Debounce vs throttle?</summary><div><p>Debounce delays execution until calls stop for a quiet period (only the last call runs). Throttle lets a call through at most once per interval, spreading executions evenly while calls continue.</p></div></details></section>"}